<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Shelley is a 51-year-old woman with focal epilepsy due to a left convexity meningioma, resected four months ago, on levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day and seizure-free since surgery. Two days ago, after a dinner party at which two other guests later fell ill, she developed nausea, six episodes of vomiting, and watery diarrhea without blood. The vomiting has eased since this morning and she is keeping down sips of water and tea. Last night she vomited about ten minutes after her evening levetiracetam tablet, and did not know whether to take another. She took this morning&apos;s dose and kept it down. She has had no tingling, twitching, or weakness of the right hand, no headache beyond a mild ache from not eating, and no confusion. She feels light-headed on standing. No recent travel or antibiotics. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago, after a shared meal</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days; vomiting easing since this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Six vomits, watery diarrhea without blood</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Mild dehydration; light-headed on standing</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Levetiracetam twice a day; one evening dose vomited within ten minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Low-grade temperature; no seizure symptoms, severe headache, or blood in the stool</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

